# Fix: Scheduled/Ended campaigns misfiled under the Active tab

## Context

`CampaignsPage.tsx` filters tabs by raw `campaign.status`, while the Status column shows `displayStatus(campaign)` (`src/lib/status.ts`), which can compute `'Scheduled'` or `'Ended'` instead of the stored value. Result: a campaign whose Status cell reads "Scheduled" or "Ended" can still be sitting under the Active (or Paused, for Ended) tab, because tab membership and the displayed label are computed independently. Confirmed via code reading — this is a real inconsistency, not a misunderstanding.

**Decision:** keep the existing 3 tabs (Active/Paused/Completed). Fold `'Ended'` into the Completed tab. Leave `'Scheduled'` campaigns under Active, unchanged.

## Change

### `src/lib/status.ts` — add a tab-grouping helper alongside `displayStatus`

